1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,413
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:02,513 --> 00:00:09,188
Today, I will talk about global warming: its causes, effects, and solutions.

3
00:00:11,388 --> 00:00:15,346
This chart shows Korea’s greenhouse gas emissions.

4
00:00:15,446 --> 00:00:23,912
In 2000, emissions were five hundred thirty-three point five million tons of carbon dioxide equivalent.

5
00:00:24,012 --> 00:00:28,890
In 2010, six hundred eighty-nine point eight.

6
00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:33,157
In 2020, seven hundred nine point five.

7
00:00:33,307 --> 00:00:37,424
And in 2023, seven hundred seven point two.

8
00:00:37,524 --> 00:00:43,390
Emissions rose sharply after 2000, and they are still high today.

9
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:49,912
Because greenhouse gases are increasing,

10
00:00:50,012 --> 00:00:52,668
our planet is getting warmer.

11
00:00:52,768 --> 00:00:57,798
Glaciers are melting, and we are seeing more floods and droughts.

12
00:00:59,998 --> 00:01:01,464
So, what can we do?

13
00:01:01,564 --> 00:01:10,930
We can use public transportation, save electricity and water, and reuse and repair our belongings.

14
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:13,512
What else can you think of?

15
00:01:17,612 --> 00:01:19,670
Let’s take action today!

16
00:01:19,770 --> 00:01:22,857
Small actions, big changes.
